{"Exported function in BackupCode.tsx is named TwoFactor which conflicts with existing TwoFactor component in TwoFactor.tsx in same directory - should be renamed to BackupCode": 0.8781502842903137, "Backup code comparison is case-sensitive - if generated codes contain letters, user entering them in different case will be incorrectly rejected": 0.6213107109069824, "Race condition in backup code validation - the backup code is read, validated, then invalidated in separate non-atomic steps, allowing concurrent requests to reuse the same one-time code": 0.8842931389808655, "First test is missing backup code dialog dismissal after fillOtp enables 2FA - the backup codes dialog must be closed before switch state can be verified, otherwise test fails or silently passes due to Promise-is-truthy bug with .isChecked()": 0.7761433124542236, "Backup codes are stored with reversible symmetric encryption instead of being hashed - since backup codes only need to be verified, each code should be individually hashed with bcrypt or salted SHA-256 to prevent exposure if CALENDSO_ENCRYPTION_KEY is leaked": 0.8520308136940002, "Password verification can be bypassed when backup code is used alongside non-empty totpCode - the password check is gated on !credentials.totpCode, so sending a dummy totpCode value skips password verification while backup code branch validates only the backup code": 0.1755802482366562, "Adding tabIndex={-1} to password toggle button removes it from keyboard tab order, making it inaccessible to keyboard-only users across all password fields site-wide": 0.9083684086799622, "req.body.backupCode is not validated to be a string before calling .replaceAll() - a non-string truthy value will throw TypeError at runtime producing unhandled 500 instead of clear 400 error": 0.8765754699707031, "Nested ternary without parentheses is hard to parse - should add explicit parentheses or refactor to helper/early-return": 0.011153018102049828, "Blob URL created via URL.createObjectURL is never revoked on component unmount, causing memory leak": 0.6101690530776978, "useState([]) is inferred as never[] by TypeScript making all subsequent operations on backupCodes type-unsafe - should add type parameter useState<string[]>([])": 0.5647240281105042, "PasswordField manages its own type internally for show/hide toggle but passing type='password' overrides that behavior since {...props} is spread after internal type, breaking the toggle": 0.02296137996017933, "Button missing type='button' attribute will default to type='submit' inside forms, causing Lost access/Go back button to trigger form submission instead of just toggling view": 0.7949415445327759, "Reset state should also clear backup codes and revoke existing object URL otherwise old download link can persist and blob URL is never cleaned up when modal is closed": 0.7447746396064758}